  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Consider the following trigonometric  equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(\\frac{x}{3})=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx={180}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot 1\\,{080}^{\u2218},\\,x={a}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot 1\\,{080}^{\u2218},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{x}{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{3}={60}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {360}^{\u2218},\\,\\frac{x}{3}={120}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {360}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\nx={180}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot 1\\,{080}^{\u2218},\\,x={360}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot 1\\,{080}^{\u2218}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=360.$",
